    /** In a template, marks it as the accessible one, so no second copy is made. */
    const val ACCESSIBLE_MARKER = "share-your-apps:accessible"

    /** Written to the root of every Store directory. */
    const val README = """SHARE YOUR APPS - DATA FOLDER

This folder holds the published contents of your Share Your Apps, the Code On
The Go plugin for sharing apps and source code with people on the same
Wi-Fi network or hotspot.

- It is managed automatically. Each time you publish, a new folder like
  this one is written and the previous one is deleted. Don't put your own
  files here.

- Anything you publish can be downloaded by anyone who can reach your store,
  and everything in this folder can be read by other apps on this device.
  Don't publish anything you want to keep private.

- To change what's published, use the Share Your Apps plugin in Code On The Go.
  Don't edit these files by hand.

- If you no longer use Share Your Apps, you can delete this folder. The store
  stops working until you publish again.

- The number in this folder's name is random. It keeps the folder from
  clashing with the name of one of your projects.
"""

